# Two DLLs with the same assembly name in one directory: run in place,
# 'dotnet exec other.dll' silently executes same.dll, because every DLL of the
# application directory is on the probing list and same.dll matches the
# assembly name (asmprinter recon 0.9). msil-run.py runs each program from a
# private copy, so each one runs its own code.

# RUN: rm -rf %t.d
# RUN: mkdir -p %t.d
# RUN: %ilasm -dll -output=%t.d/same.dll %S/Inputs/same-name-a.il
# RUN: %ilasm -dll -output=%t.d/other.dll %S/Inputs/same-name-b.il
# RUN: %msil_exec --expect %S/Inputs/same-name-b %t.d/other.dll
# RUN: %msil_exec --expect %S/Inputs/same-name-a %t.d/same.dll
